| `make test-fe-e2e` `[local]` | Runs each frontend app's browser journey, its npm script `test:e2e` (Playwright in the shipped stacks): it builds the site, serves it with the stack's own preview server on a loopback port and drives it in headless chromium, asserting what a visitor sees. | `make test-fe-e2e` | [`FE_APPS`](settings.md#make-variables), [`layers.frontend.journey.host`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`layers.frontend.journey.port`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`layers.frontend.journey.server_timeout_ms`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`layers.frontend.journey.browser_executable`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Exits 0 with no output when no frontend app is found, and exits 2, naming the app and `make fe-install`, when `npm` or `node` is not on `PATH` or an app lacks `node_modules/.package-lock.json`, npm's completion marker. Red on zero tests, a browser missing from the cache or a busy port; downloads no browser, which is `make fe-browsers`. Not for visual regression, or for the backend over a socket (`tests/e2e/`). | [limits-and-troubleshooting.md](../guides/limits-and-troubleshooting.md) | always |
